{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>ושב ה׳ אלהיך את שבותך.</b> It should have written ״והשיב את שבותך״. Our Sages learned from here: as it were, the Shekhinah dwells with Israel in the distress of their exile, and when they are redeemed, Scripture writes redemption for Himself — that He Himself returns with them. And further, one may say that the day of gathering the exiles is great and difficult, as though He Himself must literally take hold with His hands, each man from his place — as in what is written (Isaiah 27): ״ואתם תלקטו לאחד אחד בני ישראל״, and so we find regarding the exiles of the other nations as well (Jeremiah 48): ״ושבתי שבות מואב״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:55.566144975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}